    title: 'Collected from your Nairobi address',
    body: 'Your guide arrives at your hotel, apartment or airport terminal at the time confirmed by email. Early departures matter here, because the drive to the main gate crosses the southern side of the city and Nairobi traffic builds quickly after 7am.',
  },
  {
    time: 'At the gate',
    title: 'Entry formalities at Nairobi National Park',
    body: 'Kenya Wildlife Service takes entry payment per person per day at the gate. Your guide handles the paperwork while you get your camera ready, so the group is on the plains rather than in a queue.',
  },
  {
    time: 'Morning',
    title: 'The plains, the dams and the gorge',
    body: 'The route follows where wildlife has been moving that week: the open Athi plains for lion, zebra and eland, the dams for hippo and waterbirds, and the Mokoyeti gorge and Hyena Dam circuits when the grass is high. Your guide adjusts the loop on the morning rather than repeating a fixed circuit.',
  },
  {
    time: 'Mid morning',
    title: 'A stop with the skyline behind you',
    body: 'A pause at a permitted viewpoint for coffee and the photograph most visitors come for: grazing herds in the foreground and Nairobi towers on the horizon, which no other national park in the world offers.',
  },
  {
    time: 'Return',
    title: 'Back to your door, or on to the afternoon',
    body: 'Half-day guests are dropped back in time for lunch. Guests combining the park with the elephant orphanage, the Giraffe Centre and Karen continue straight from the gate, because those attractions sit minutes from the park boundary.',
  },
];

const included = [
  'Private vehicle with a pop-up roof for game viewing and photography',
  'Professional driver guide who knows the park circuits',
  'Door-to-door pick-up and drop-off in Nairobi, JKIA or Wilson Airport',
  'Drinking water on board',
  '[PLACEHOLDER: confirm whether binoculars, snacks or a picnic breakfast are included]',
